# Recon: Stripe Billing (test mode)

Owner: main session. Step 1 of the replication playbook. Run on 2026-09-23 with
`recon/recon.sh` (raw responses in `recon/out/`, not committed: they carry account IDs).

## What was done

On a test clock frozen at `1790000000` (2026-09-21T14:13:20Z): one product with two monthly
prices (10 USD, 30 USD), a 20 % forever coupon, one customer with `pm_card_visa`, one subscription
on the 10 USD price. Then `POST /v1/invoices/create_preview` for an upgrade to 30 USD at
`proration_date = T0 + 10 days`, with and without the coupon, each run twice. Then a Customer
Portal configuration and two portal sessions (home, and the `subscription_update_confirm` deep link).

## Observed

- **Preview is deterministic except for IDs.** Diffing the two runs field by field, only `id`,
  `lines.data[].id`, `lines.data[].invoice`, `...invoice_item` and `lines.url` differ. Noise mask
  candidates: every `*_id`-like path with prefixes `upcoming_in_`, `il_tmp_`, `ii_`, `di_`.
- **Proration arithmetic, 20 of 30 days remaining:**
  - credit for unused time on the old price: `-667` (1000 × 20/30 = 666.67, rounded to 667);
  - charge for remaining time on the new price: `2000`;
  - next full period on the new price: `3000`;
  - `subtotal = total = amount_due = 4333`.
- **Coupon interaction (20 % off), a quirk worth a rule:** the remaining-time line is discounted
  inside the line (`1600`, description "avec 20.0% off"), the unused-time credit is not discounted
  (`-667`), and the next-period line is discounted at invoice level (`total_discount_amounts = 600`).
  Result: `subtotal 3933`, `total 3333`.
- **Billing mode:** new subscriptions default to `billing_mode.type = flexible` with
  `proration_discounts = included`. The docs describe `classic` as giving different totals for the
  same sequence: a parameter of the slice, not a constant.
- **Line descriptions follow the account or customer locale** (French here). Either set
  `preferred_locales` on the customer or mask descriptions: a noise source unrelated to logic.
- **Portal configuration rules, found by error messages** (awkward cases a faithful clone must reproduce):
  - "For each product, its price must have unique billing intervals" → the plan switch needs one
    product per plan.
  - "Cannot enable subscription updates while payment method update is disabled."
- **Portal sessions** (home and update-confirm deep link) are created by API; URLs point to
  `billing.stripe.com`.

## Portal (recorded with `recon/portal.ts`, Playwright headless)

- **The confirmation screen does not show the proration.** It shows the new plan, "What you'll pay
  monthly starting October 21, 2026 $30.00", the card, and a "Subscribe and pay" button. The info
  icon's tooltip says: "This estimate covers recurring charges. One-time adjustments, like
  prorations and credits, will appear on your final invoice." An awkward behaviour to reproduce
  as is.
- **The proration is in the traffic, not on screen.** The page calls
  `GET billing.stripe.com/v1/billing_portal/sessions/<bps>/update_preview`, which returns
  `latest_invoice`, `upcoming_invoice`, `recurring_invoice`, `generates_immediate_invoice`,
  `reset_billing_cycle_anchor`, `schedule_update_at_period_end`. At clock time T0 (whole period
  unused) `upcoming_invoice` = `-1000 + 3000 + 3000 = 5000`, `generates_immediate_invoice = false`:
  the proration is billed at the next renewal, not now.
- The portal page calls `api.hcaptcha.com/checksiteconfig`; no challenge was shown in test mode.
- The aria snapshot contains the session secret in a link URL: scrubbing must cover snapshots,
  not only HAR headers (R-27).
- Chrome headless opened in `en-US` still shows the account name in French: account-level
  strings are data, not locale.

## Still open

1. Dashboard- and portal-specific terms (only the Services Agreement was read).
2. Rounding rule: one case (666.67 → 667) is consistent with half-up and with half-even. A probe
   landing exactly on .5 is needed.
3. Portal screens before and after confirmation (plan list, success state) not yet captured.
# Analysis plan: stripe-billing, holdout batch 3

Pre-registered on 2026-10-13 and committed before any fixture of the batch is recorded (rule 3 of
`docs/verification.md`). Nothing below may change once the first `hold-b3-` fixture exists; a
change means a new batch with a new seed.

## The batch

- **Probes:** `hold-b3-001` to `hold-b3-473`, generated by `wideProbesV2` in `probes.ts` from the
  `hold-b3` seed in `holdout-seed.json`, drawn when this plan was written. Every `hold-` probe is
  holdout by construction (`splitOf`); the seed file never enters a builder sandbox.
- **Distribution:** `WIDE_DISTRIBUTION_V2` in `probes.ts`: the slice 1 change of batches 1 and 2,
  widened where breaker round 1 found the clone failing (up to 4 items, amounts from 50 cents to
  $100,000 on a log scale, percent coupons up to 100 %, amount-off coupons up to $10,000,
  quantity 0, interval changes on any item count) and drawing fewer easy cases (the `none`
  behaviour 5 % instead of 15 %; most changes that would change nothing become quantity changes).
  The builder may train on the 300 `wide3-` probes drawn from it (their dev share).
- **Recording:** once, with `npm run record`, Stripe test mode, each probe twice for noise.
- **Size:** 473, as for batch 2: below 1 % at 99 % with no failure, below 1 % at 95 % with one.

## The claim and the decision rule

- **Claim under test:** on `WIDE_DISTRIBUTION_V2`, the clone's per-case divergence rate is below
  1 %.
- **A case passes** when `npm run verify` finds no blocking difference under `policy.json` as
  locked at the measurement commit. A crash counts as a failure. Any change to `policy.json`
  between this plan and the measurement is listed in the fidelity report.
- **Decision**, with k failures out of 473 and one-sided exact (Clopper-Pearson) upper bounds:
  - k = 0: "below 1 % at 99 % confidence" (bound 0.97 %);
  - k = 1: "below 1 % at 95 % confidence" (bound 0.999 %), not at 99 %;
  - k ≥ 2: the claim is not supported; report "k of 473" and both bounds.
- **Reported apart, no claim:** the share of easy cases (Stripe errors, changes that change
  nothing) and the result on the others.

## The measurement

- **Measured clone:** the clone measured on batch 2 (`claim-batch-2`), after one more builder pass
  in the agent container that may use every dev fixture (the breaker's, the mutation-testing
  probes, `wide3-`) and never sees batch 3. The clone is frozen at a commit before batch 3 is
  scored.
- **One look:** `npm run verify stripe-billing -- --split holdout` runs once on that commit. Its
  line in `verify/runs.jsonl` is the result; the fidelity report checks that this plan was
  committed before the batch. A run that stops before scoring may be repeated; a scored run
  counts.
- **Afterwards the batch is spent.** The result goes into `measurements.md`, whatever it is.
/**
 * Stripe Billing adapter. One probe = a fresh billing world on its own test clock (product,
 * prices, coupons, customer, subscription), then one `create_preview` of the probed change. The
 * same code runs against Stripe test mode and against the clone: only the SDK's host changes.
 */
import { existsSync, readFileSync } from "node:fs";
import { join } from "node:path";
import Stripe from "stripe";
import { z } from "zod";
import type { Probe, Side, TargetAdapter } from "../../harness/src/adapter.ts";
import { JsonSchema, type Json } from "../../harness/src/json.ts";
import { probes } from "./probes.ts";
import { LifeInput, runLifecycle } from "./lifecycle.ts";
import { ExploreInput, runExplore } from "./explore.ts";
import { runWalkthrough, UiInput } from "./ui.ts";
import { runWide, WideInput } from "./wide.ts";

const Coupon = z.object({
  percent_off: z.number().optional(),
  amount_off: z.number().optional(),
  duration: z.enum(["forever", "once"]),
});
const Plan = z.object({ amount: z.number(), interval: z.enum(["month", "year"]) });
const Input = z.object({
  start: z.number(),
  billing_mode: z.enum(["flexible", "classic"]),
  plan: Plan,
  quantity: z.number(),
  coupon: Coupon.nullable(),
  change: z.object({
    plan: Plan.nullable(),
    quantity: z.number().nullable(),
    offset: z.number(),
    proration_behavior: z.enum(["create_prorations", "none", "always_invoice"]).nullable(),
    discount: Coupon.nullable(),
  }),
});

// The key comes from STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, else from the file named by STRIPE_ENV, else from .env at
// the repository root (git-ignored).
export function testKey(): string {
  const file = process.env.STRIPE_ENV ?? join(import.meta.dirname, "..", "..", ".env");
  const fromFile = existsSync(file)
    ? /STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=(\S+)/.exec(readFileSync(file, "utf8"))?.[1]
    : undefined;
  const key = process.env.STRIPE_SECRET_KEY ?? fromFile;
  // Invariant 4: never record outside test mode.
  if (key?.startsWith("sk_test_") !== true) {
    throw new Error("refusing: STRIPE_SECRET_KEY is missing or not a test key (see .env.example)");
  }
  return key;
}

export function client(side: Side): Stripe {
  if (side.kind === "target") return new Stripe(testKey(), { maxNetworkRetries: 2 });
  const url = new URL(side.url);
  return new Stripe("sk_test_clone", {
    host: url.hostname,
    port: Number(url.port),
    protocol: "http",
  });
}

const toJson = (v: unknown): Json => JsonSchema.parse(JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(v)));

function errorJson(e: unknown): Json {
  if (e instanceof Stripe.errors.StripeError) {
    return {
      error: { type: e.type, code: e.code ?? null, param: e.param ?? null, message: e.message },
    };
  }
  throw e;
}

async function couponId(stripe: Stripe, c: z.infer<typeof Coupon>): Promise<string> {
  const created = await stripe.coupons.create({
    duration: c.duration,
    ...(c.percent_off !== undefined ? { percent_off: c.percent_off } : {}),
    ...(c.amount_off !== undefined ? { amount_off: c.amount_off, currency: "usd" } : {}),
  });
  return created.id;
}

async function run(probe: Probe, side: Side): Promise<Record<string, Json>> {
  const ui = UiInput.safeParse(probe.input);
  if (ui.success) return runWalkthrough(client(side), ui.data);
  const explore = ExploreInput.safeParse(probe.input);
  if (explore.success) return runExplore(client(side), explore.data);
  const wide = WideInput.safeParse(probe.input);
  if (wide.success) return runWide(client(side), wide.data, toJson, errorJson);
  const life = LifeInput.safeParse(probe.input);
  if (life.success) return runLifecycle(client(side), life.data);
  const p = Input.parse(probe.input);
  const stripe = client(side);
  const clock = await stripe.testHelpers.testClocks.create({ frozen_time: p.start });
  const price = async (plan: z.infer<typeof Plan>, name: string): Promise<string> => {
    const product = await stripe.products.create({ name });
    const created = await stripe.prices.create({
      product: product.id,
      currency: "usd",
      unit_amount: plan.amount,
      recurring: { interval: plan.interval },
    });
    return created.id;
  };
  const oldPrice = await price(p.plan, "Basic");
  const newPrice = p.change.plan ? await price(p.change.plan, "Pro") : null;
  const customer = await stripe.customers.create({
    test_clock: clock.id,
    payment_method: "pm_card_visa",
    invoice_settings: { default_payment_method: "pm_card_visa" },
    preferred_locales: ["en"],
  });
  const subscription = await stripe.subscriptions.create({
    customer: customer.id,
    items: [{ price: oldPrice, quantity: p.quantity }],
    billing_mode: { type: p.billing_mode },
    ...(p.coupon ? { discounts: [{ coupon: await couponId(stripe, p.coupon) }] } : {}),
  });
  const item = subscription.items.data[0];
  if (!item) throw new Error("subscription created without an item");
  const discount = p.change.discount ? await couponId(stripe, p.change.discount) : null;

  let preview: Json;
  try {
    preview = toJson(
      await stripe.invoices.createPreview({
        subscription: subscription.id,
        subscription_details: {
          items: [
            {
              id: item.id,
              ...(newPrice !== null ? { price: newPrice } : {}),
              ...(p.change.quantity !== null ? { quantity: p.change.quantity } : {}),
            },
          ],
          proration_date: p.start + p.change.offset,
          ...(p.change.proration_behavior !== null
            ? { proration_behavior: p.change.proration_behavior }
            : {}),
        },
        ...(discount !== null ? { discounts: [{ coupon: discount }] } : {}),
      }),
    );
  } catch (e) {
    preview = errorJson(e);
  }
  const first =
    typeof subscription.latest_invoice === "string" ? subscription.latest_invoice : null;
  const invoice = first !== null ? await stripe.invoices.retrieve(first) : null;
  return {
    preview,
    first_invoice: invoice
      ? {
          subtotal: invoice.subtotal,
          total: invoice.total,
          amount_due: invoice.amount_due,
          status: invoice.status,
        }
      : null,
  };
}

const recordedWith = (): Record<string, Json> => ({
  stripe_api_version: Stripe.API_VERSION,
  stripe_node: Stripe.PACKAGE_VERSION,
});

const adapter: TargetAdapter = { probes, run, cloneEntry: "clone/server.ts", recordedWith };
export default adapter;

/**
 * The widened slice-1 probe: the same mid-cycle change previewed with `create_preview`, on a
 * subscription of one to three items sharing a monthly or yearly interval, with up to two
 * coupons. The original single-item probe is the special case of one item and at most one coupon;
 * it keeps its own input shape so that its recorded fixtures stay valid.
 */
import type Stripe from "stripe";
import { z } from "zod";
import type { Json } from "../../harness/src/json.ts";

export const Coupon = z.object({
  percent_off: z.number().optional(),
  amount_off: z.number().optional(),
  duration: z.enum(["forever", "once"]),
});
export type Coupon = z.infer<typeof Coupon>;

const Interval = z.enum(["month", "year"]);

export const WideInput = z.object({
  kind: z.literal("wide"),
  start: z.number(),
  billing_mode: z.enum(["flexible", "classic"]),
  interval: Interval,
  items: z
    .array(z.object({ amount: z.number(), quantity: z.number() }))
    .min(1)
    .max(4),
  coupons: z.array(Coupon).max(2),
  change: z.object({
    item: z.number().int().min(0),
    amount: z.number().nullable(),
    // Only with a single item: a subscription's items share one interval.
    interval: Interval.nullable(),
    quantity: z.number().nullable(),
    offset: z.number(),
    proration_behavior: z.enum(["create_prorations", "none", "always_invoice"]).nullable(),
    discount: Coupon.nullable(),
  }),
});
export type WideInput = z.infer<typeof WideInput>;

export async function couponId(stripe: Stripe, c: Coupon): Promise<string> {
  const created = await stripe.coupons.create({
    duration: c.duration,
    ...(c.percent_off !== undefined ? { percent_off: c.percent_off } : {}),
    ...(c.amount_off !== undefined ? { amount_off: c.amount_off, currency: "usd" } : {}),
  });
  return created.id;
}

export async function runWide(
  stripe: Stripe,
  p: WideInput,
  toJson: (v: unknown) => Json,
  errorJson: (e: unknown) => Json,
): Promise<Record<string, Json>> {
  const clock = await stripe.testHelpers.testClocks.create({ frozen_time: p.start });
  const price = async (amount: number, interval: "month" | "year", name: string) => {
    const product = await stripe.products.create({ name });
    const created = await stripe.prices.create({
      product: product.id,
      currency: "usd",
      unit_amount: amount,
      recurring: { interval },
    });
    return created.id;
  };
  const names = ["Plan A", "Plan B", "Plan C"];
  const prices: string[] = [];
  for (const [i, item] of p.items.entries())
    prices.push(await price(item.amount, p.interval, names[i] ?? "Plan"));
  const changed = p.items[p.change.item];
  if (!changed) throw new Error(`change.item ${String(p.change.item)} is out of range`);
  const newPrice =
    p.change.amount !== null || p.change.interval !== null
      ? await price(p.change.amount ?? changed.amount, p.change.interval ?? p.interval, "Plan New")
      : null;
  const customer = await stripe.customers.create({
    test_clock: clock.id,
    payment_method: "pm_card_visa",
    invoice_settings: { default_payment_method: "pm_card_visa" },
    preferred_locales: ["en"],
  });
  const discounts: { coupon: string }[] = [];
  for (const c of p.coupons) discounts.push({ coupon: await couponId(stripe, c) });
  const subscription = await stripe.subscriptions.create({
    customer: customer.id,
    items: p.items.map((item, i) => ({ price: prices[i] ?? "", quantity: item.quantity })),
    billing_mode: { type: p.billing_mode },
    ...(discounts.length > 0 ? { discounts } : {}),
  });
  const target = subscription.items.data.find((i) => i.price.id === prices[p.change.item]);
  if (!target) throw new Error("subscription created without the changed item");
  const discount = p.change.discount ? await couponId(stripe, p.change.discount) : null;

  let preview: Json;
  try {
    preview = toJson(
      await stripe.invoices.createPreview({
        subscription: subscription.id,
        subscription_details: {
          items: [
            {
              id: target.id,
              ...(newPrice !== null ? { price: newPrice } : {}),
              ...(p.change.quantity !== null ? { quantity: p.change.quantity } : {}),
            },
          ],
          proration_date: p.start + p.change.offset,
          ...(p.change.proration_behavior !== null
            ? { proration_behavior: p.change.proration_behavior }
            : {}),
        },
        ...(discount !== null ? { discounts: [{ coupon: discount }] } : {}),
      }),
    );
  } catch (e) {
    preview = errorJson(e);
  }
  const first =
    typeof subscription.latest_invoice === "string" ? subscription.latest_invoice : null;
  const invoice = first !== null ? await stripe.invoices.retrieve(first) : null;
  return {
    preview,
    first_invoice: invoice
      ? {
          subtotal: invoice.subtotal,
          total: invoice.total,
          amount_due: invoice.amount_due,
          status: invoice.status,
        }
      : null,
  };
}

